From b4f12793a37b3d815298ee1944e1cd73590edc6c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alessandro Fontana <alessandro.fontana@pm.me>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 20:05:38 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 15/31] android: Add flash LED support

A camera may name its flash LED, a LED class device, in the HAL
configuration file. The HAL then reports a flash unit and the flash AE
modes, and drives the LED through sysfs:

- set_torch_mode() switches the torch and reports the torch status
  through the callbacks. The torch is not available while the camera
  is open.
- FLASH_MODE_TORCH turns the LED on.
- For still captures with AE_MODE_ON_ALWAYS_FLASH, or ON_AUTO_FLASH in
  a dark scene, the LED stays on from the AE precapture trigger to the
  end of the capture. Without a strobe synchronised with the exposure,
  as with a software ISP, the AE adapts to the LED during the
  precapture sequence.

Assisted-by: LLM
